{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block main %}
<h1>Our rules</h1>
<p class="lede">Eight rules that keep this site neutral. They apply to everyone, including whoever pays for it.</p>
<ol class="rules">
  <li><strong>Coverage is never sold.</strong> No one can pay to be covered, to be left out, or to have a place or body added sooner.</li>
  <li><strong>Places are added by a published rule.</strong> First, other bodies that serve residents we already cover. Then adjoining counties, largest first. Then any place where 100 or more residents ask for it.</li>
  <li><strong>Payers get no say over content.</strong> No editing, delaying, hiding, advance review or &ldquo;added context&rdquo;.</li>
  <li><strong>Every official and place is shown the same way, by a published method.</strong> See <a href="{{ root }}method.html">Method</a> and the rules on <a href="{{ root }}about.html">About</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>One corrections policy for everyone.</strong> See <a href="{{ root }}corrections.html">Corrections</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Every page links the official record.</strong> Each record page says &ldquo;Unofficial copy&rdquo; and links the official source, and each fact links the page of the document it came from.</li>
  <li><strong>Every payer is listed, with conflict checks.</strong> Name, amount and contract appear on <a href="{{ root }}who-runs-this.html">Who runs this</a>. Conflicts are checked before an agreement is signed.</li>
  <li><strong>Free coverage continues for at least 12 months after a payer leaves, and we sign only our own service agreement.</strong> We do not sign a payer's terms.</li>
</ol>
{% endblock %}
